### 3.1 Borehole Environment, Bad-Hole Flagging & Normalization Criteria

* **Bad-Hole Criteria Applied:** Caliper washout $> {{ qaqc_params.caliper_limit }}\text{ in}$ above bit size (`{{ qaqc_params.bitsize_in }}\text{ in}`), Density correction $\Delta\rho > {{ qaqc_params.drho_limit }}\text{ g/cc}$, or density washout $\rho_b < {{ qaqc_params.rhob_min }}\text{ g/cc}$.
* **Bad-Hole Mitigation Mode:** `{{ qaqc_params.badhole_treatment }}` (shale/porosity fallback in rugose washouts to prevent optimistic density porosity spikes).
* **Hydrocarbon Light-Fluid Correction:** Gaymard-Poupon crossplot rotation applied where $\rho_{hc} = {{ qaqc_params.rho_hc }}\text{ g/cc}$ and $HI_{hc} = {{ qaqc_params.hi_hc }}$.
* **Normalization Method:** {{ qaqc_params.norm_method }} across target reservoir zones.

